virtuoso-cli-integration
========================

Combined, experimental toolset for driving one Cadence Virtuoso session
from two open-source bridges without them fighting over it.

Built from (both MIT-licensed):

  * virtuoso-cli (vcli) by deanyou
    https://github.com/deanyou/virtuoso-cli
    Base of this repository (fork, MIT license retained in LICENSE).

  * virtuoso-bridge-lite by Arcadia-1 (Tsinghua University /
    tokenzhang.com)
    https://github.com/Arcadia-1/virtuoso-bridge-lite
    Vendored in python/ (MIT license retained in python/LICENSE) with
    the cross-bridge lock applied in-tree; see python/VENDORED.md.
    If you use virtuoso-bridge in academic work, cite Zhang et al. 2025
    (see python/CITATION.cff).

Both upstream projects descend from the same "RAMIC Bridge" SKILL daemon,
which is exactly why they collide when loaded into one Virtuoso session;
this repo exists to fix that.
